{
  "note": [
    "The corpus both implementations of the feature-plan validator are run against.",
    "",
    "`tool/feature_plan.dart` in this project and `scripts/feature-plan.mjs` in",
    "create-react-app are the same validator written twice, in two languages, for",
    "two dialects of the same schema. Two implementations of one contract drift;",
    "these cases are what stops them drifting silently.",
    "",
    "Only cases both dialects must agree on live here. The archetype vocabularies",
    "differ on purpose \u2014 this app's five are mobile shapes and React's four are",
    "page shapes \u2014 so every case uses `form`, which both declare, and the",
    "archetype-specific rules are tested separately on each side.",
    "",
    "`match` is a substring that must appear in the rejection message. It is",
    "deliberately the part both implementations word identically: a shared corpus",
    "that also fixes the prose would stop either side improving an error message."
  ],
  "cases": [
    {
      "case": "valid",
      "expect": "accept",
      "match": null,
      "why": "The shape both dialects agree is a plan: a form surface, one column of fields, a named peak and end, all four states, a justified control and an overlay the kit owns.",
      "plan": {
        "feature": {
          "id": "shared-case",
          "title": "Shared case",
          "problem": "The two implementations of this validator have to agree, and nothing checked that they did."
        },
        "surfaces": [
          {
            "id": "s1",
            "name": "Details",
            "archetype": "form",
            "primaryAction": "Save",
            "panels": [
              {
                "fields": [
